   :operational-c6-requires-c5-bindings-core-interface-can-precede-resolution,
   :qualification
   "D1 places Core Gravity AST before Name Resolution; C1 places resolve-names before lower-to-core. C5 resolves syntax after expansion and before type/effects; C6 explicitly consumes resolved syntax and C5 bindings. Use that actual C6 consumer edge without requiring completed semantic Core for Resolve. Whether D1 means the identical AST construction event remains an explicit architecture-owner qualification; no source rewrite or invented fused pass."}
  {:id :legacy-project-accounting-wording,
